[sliver] Set aside by Derek: "I don't love it. But it's not the highest priority problem." These six faces bound the outer fore coils' 1.35 mm clearance pockets at the selected aligned pump, tee and valve stations.
alternatives: Moving each complete fore group 1.6 mm inboard removes these pocket boundaries and changes its pump seats, straight upper receiving links and lower returns. The small lower-elbow contacts involve flexible metal tabs, which Derek explicitly permits to bend; they are not rigid coil interferences. Moving only an outer valve or tee changes a straight receiving link. Moving the whole flank to the pocket floor changes the seam rail and funnel-frame grooves. The selected arrangement retains the named coil clearances and Derek's stated cosmetic priority.
